\tag{fdip}
\title{Exchanging the two parts of a graded coupling}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The inversion in \ref{fdip-013T} exchanges the signs of a
grading. What happens if the two sign spaces carry different
representations of an internal group? Can conjugating scalars
make an exchange possible?}

\p{Even when both signs carry the same representation, a
coupling can act differently on them. Which equations decide
whether a given inversion or charge conjugation transports that
coupling to the one specified at the new background?}

